      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either the previous content if the file existed, or a record that it didn\u0027t exist. If the agent run fails (due to a turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every write in reverse order: restoring prior content or deleting newly created files. This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log for a single run.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent doesn\u0027t use this rollback functionality since it has no write tool, but the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library for agents that do write.",
      "input_tokens": 5357,
      "output_tokens": 195
